"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics and optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility. The project was initially introduced with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th (or July 15th in one update) and Q3 2023, with Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole mentioned as leads. A budget of $500,000 was allocated for phase one, and later, the compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000. The team expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with an onboarding session set for September 10th. Key milestones include the completion of the design phase, the testing phase, and a celebration scheduled for October 10th. The project is currently moving into the development phase under the guidance of lead developer Omar Jensen. The team is also gathering ideas to leverage AI in data visualization tools, with proposals due by July 20th, and is seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November."
